  <title id="bdl27booutofdomain-title">Top-1 target value against the number of molecules queried on four out-of-domain tasks</title>
  <desc id="bdl27booutofdomain-desc">Four panels, each with a dashed line at the optimum. (a) Molecular docking, binding score, lower is better: ADKF-IFT reaches the optimum near minus 12.3 after about 13 queries; GNN-MT, ProtoNet and PAR drop fast but level off near minus 11.9 to minus 12.2; the fingerprint representation improves slowest and ends near minus 11.1. (b) Antibiotic discovery, relative growth, lower is better: ADKF-IFT and ProtoNet reach the optimum near 0.04 after about 6 queries, DKT, PAR and GNN-MT after about 14, CNP and fingerprint end near 0.23 and MAT near 0.77. (c) Antiviral drug design, pIC50 fluorescence, higher is better: MAT and GNN-MT reach the optimum 8.57 after about 13 to 22 queries; ADKF-IFT reaches about 8.35, CNP about 8.2, DKT about 7.7 and fingerprint, ProtoNet and PAR about 7.3 to 7.8 after 30 queries. (d) Material design, power conversion efficiency, higher is better: ADKF-IFT rises fastest, above 10 after about 4 queries, and all representations approach about 10.5 to 10.9 by 40 queries, below the optimum 11.07.</desc>
